  "body": "FanHub hid onboarding guidance before the server confirmed persistence and allowed old-session responses to affect a returning account. This increment keeps guidance until a validated terminal receipt, provides localized retry/status, captures the initiating credential and coalesces duplicate close commands. Guest/manager tips remain ephemeral and never invent a first useful action.\n\nStacked on #421. Reuses the bounded onboarding work from #368 at ff3cd1676a6db7b6ceef56d44407b0846a4f2071 without merging its unrelated event stack. Keeps the existing component tests and adapts obsolete per-party error replay to the current-session contract.\n\nValidation: 212 suites / 2,031 web tests; typecheck, focused lint and repository quality pass. Fourteen isolated browser cases pass across Chromium desktop/phone/tablet, Firefox and WebKit; keyboard recovery, malformed replies, synthetic return visit and axe serious/critical checks. TLC safety and conditional liveness explore 215 distinct states; four invariant mutants and one unfair liveness control fail as intended. Full event runner passes ten positive configurations, eight expected negative controls, Alloy one SAT scenario/eight UNSAT assertions. Bounds, assumptions, implementation conformance, screenshot and logs: [audit evidence](docs/ux-ui-audit/2026-09-17/fanhub-onboarding.md).\n\nNo API schema, migration or mobile gitlink change. Revert this web increment to roll back; do not delete server progress. Exact-head hosted checks/review remain required. Production merge/release is held while the user-confirmed concurrent deployment continues. These fixtures do not establish real backend persistence, complete accessibility compliance or mobile publication.\n",
